Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P9.7 Options row in the field menu (the port options screen in game, slice 1)

P9.7, slice 1 (the field, not battle yet): the field menu's option list gets
one more row, Options, just above Return to title (P6.27, patch 0123), in the
game's font, five EU languages (one on US). Cross on it opens the port
options screen over the menu (port/options/field_options.c; the native
overlay draws the same Options window it shows on the title). The menu task
waits while it is open (the field menu is already a paused state), hands it
the pad each frame and takes the pad back when Triangle closes it. Rows that
cannot change safely in game are greyed (Widescreen, the Cheats screen).
Without the native overlay nothing is added (dw3_port_field_options_enabled()
is 0).

The options panel has a sprite for five rows (0x1C) and six (0x1B). With the
two port rows that is seven and, with the card folders row, eight, so the
panel's bottom edge is covered and redrawn lower by drawFieldMenuPanelRow,
now for any number of extra rows (patch 0123 drew exactly one).
FieldMenuWindows.options grows from seven to eight windows (PORT_HOST only).

